  "user": "Please look up transaction TX-0401 in my account records and verify its amount. Then explain which reason codes could apply; I have not yet told you what happened.",
  "answer": "I found TX-0401 on account ACC-1005 (EUR).\n\n**TX-0401 details**\n- **Amount:** EUR 240.00, confirmed in your records\n- **Merchant:** TechMart Online\n- **Date:** 2026-07-20\n- **Type:** Card payment, outgoing\n- **Status:** Settled\n\nI also see **TX-0402**, dated 2026-07-14, for the same amount (EUR 240.00) to the same merchant, TechMart Online, and also settled.\n\n**Reason codes that could apply**\n\nWhich code fits depends on what happened. Based on the records, these are the possibilities:\n\n1. **duplicate_charge**: This fits if you were charged twice for one purchase. TX-0401 and TX-0402 match in amount and merchant, so this is worth checking first.\n2. **unauthorized_debit**: This fits if you did not make or authorize either payment.\n3. **fraud_card_not_present**: This fits if the card was used online without your authorization, which is consistent with a card payment to an online merchant.\n4. **goods_not_received**: This fits if you paid for an item that was never delivered.\n5. **service_not_rendered**: This fits if you paid for a service that was not provided.\n\nPlease tell me what happened with TX-0401. If you were charged twice, I can check whether a duplicate-charge dispute is eligible. I will not open anything until you confirm the details and the eligibility check passes.",
